Venetium 0054 - stop treating every 2 GB machine as permanently short of memory, and stop rebuilding the D3D9 swap chain.
From the performance research (C:\handoff\PERF-RESEARCH.md, 2026-10-15; items M1, V1, G1), his "fix all".
- components/memory_pressure (M1): Windows declares MODERATE pressure below 1000 MiB of available RAM and CRITICAL below
  400 MiB, whatever the machine has. A 2 GB tablet therefore sits at MODERATE nearly all the time - the Surface 2's
  first-release log has 515 of 525 Memory.PressureLevel2 samples at moderate - which keeps the spare renderer away,
  cuts the GPU caches to a quarter, prunes the back/forward cache and halves discardable memory every 5-10 s. Below
  4 GiB of RAM the thresholds now scale with the installed memory (moderate = RAM/4, at least 300 MiB; critical =
  RAM/10, at least 150 MiB: about 512/205 MiB at 2 GiB); 4 GiB and up keep 1000/400.
- content/renderer/render_process_impl.cc (V1): on desktop "low end" means up to 2 GiB, and every renderer there got
  V8's --optimize-for-size: a 1 MiB young generation (about 16 MiB otherwise at 2 GiB) and the heap in permanent
  memory-saver mode (minimal growth, compaction on every mark-compact). Off Android it now sets only
  --max-semi-space-size=8, the value V8 itself picks for non-high-end Android. Android keeps the old flag.
- components/viz/.../skia_output_device_gl.cc (G1): without DirectComposition (the Tegra) viz toggles the GL swap
  interval: vsync off for the first 59 frames, then on, and off/on again around every menu, tooltip or dropdown. On
  ANGLE's D3D9 backend each interval change recreates the swap chain on the next swap (SurfaceD3D mSwapIntervalDirty ->
  SwapChain9::reset: a full-window render target reallocated and copied). On ANGLE D3D9 the interval is now set once,
  to off (the state the tracker uses whenever several windows swap); frames stay paced by the GPU vsync BeginFrame
  source and windowed DWM presents do not tear. Other backends unchanged.
Device: not yet measured on hardware; the thresholds and the V8 size are tunable in one place each.

diff --git a/components/memory_pressure/system_memory_pressure_evaluator_win.cc b/components/memory_pressure/system_memory_pressure_evaluator_win.cc
index 7a4c90e..9b280f8 100644
--- a/components/memory_pressure/system_memory_pressure_evaluator_win.cc
+++ b/components/memory_pressure/system_memory_pressure_evaluator_win.cc
@@ -125,13 +125,32 @@ void MemoryPressureWatcherDelegate::OnObjectSignaled(HANDLE handle) {
   std::move(callback_).Run();
 }
 
+// Venetium 0054: the fixed 1000/400 MiB available-RAM thresholds keep a 2 GB
+// machine at MODERATE pressure nearly all the time (Surface 2: 98% of
+// Memory.PressureLevel2 samples), which keeps the spare renderer away, cuts
+// the GPU caches to a quarter and prunes the back/forward cache every 5-10 s.
+// Below 4 GiB of RAM scale them with the installed memory (2 GiB: about
+// 512/205 MiB); at 4 GiB and above they stay at the upstream values.
+base::ByteCount ScaledThreshold(base::ByteCount upstream,
+                                int64_t total_mib_divisor,
+                                int64_t floor_mib) {
+  const int64_t total_mib =
+      base::SysInfo::AmountOfTotalPhysicalMemory().InMiB();
+  if (total_mib <= 0 || total_mib >= 4096) {
+    return upstream;
+  }
+  return base::MiB(std::clamp<int64_t>(total_mib / total_mib_divisor,
+                                       floor_mib, upstream.InMiB()));
+}
+
 }  // namespace
 
 SystemMemoryPressureEvaluator::SystemMemoryPressureEvaluator(
     std::unique_ptr<MemoryPressureVoter> voter)
-    : SystemMemoryPressureEvaluator(kPhysicalMemoryDefaultModerateThreshold,
-                                    kPhysicalMemoryDefaultCriticalThreshold,
-                                    std::move(voter)) {}
+    : SystemMemoryPressureEvaluator(
+          ScaledThreshold(kPhysicalMemoryDefaultModerateThreshold, 4, 300),
+          ScaledThreshold(kPhysicalMemoryDefaultCriticalThreshold, 10, 150),
+          std::move(voter)) {}
 
 SystemMemoryPressureEvaluator::SystemMemoryPressureEvaluator(
     base::ByteCount moderate_threshold,
